{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3529,3645p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; sed -n '3937,3968p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; sed -n '1,230p' test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_test.clj; rg -n \\\"php/call|php/resolve-fn|php/callable|yang.call|:php/type :closure|:php/type.*function\\\" src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc test/yang/php/antlr\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3529,3645p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; sed -n '3937,3968p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; sed -n '1,230p' test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_test.clj; rg -n \\\"php/call|php/resolve-fn|php/callable|yang.call|:php/type :closure|:php/type.*function\\\" src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc test/yang/php/antlr\"","aggregated_output":"Every supported source-level callable, after its source-required\nresolution, exposes `:yang.call/entry`, an ordinary Yin closure taking\nexactly one invocation record. Invoking it is an ordinary\n`:application`. No AST tag, lambda slot, instruction, host primitive,\neffect kind, or source-language test is added to the VM.\n\nThis is an internal calling convention, not a transport, another system\nABI, or a host callback interface. Calls between source languages inside\none task do not themselves cross a host boundary. Portable I/O and\ncross-task interaction continue through `dao.stream`.\n\n**Transparent calling** means that an admitted callable can be passed,\nstored, returned, and invoked by any conforming frontend without a\nhandwritten language-pair wrapper. It does not mean every foreign value\nsatisfies every source operation. Invocation, name visibility, and value\ninterpretation are distinct obligations.\n\nThe convention covers ordinary source calls and supported callable\nobjects, including higher-order calls. It does not make macros runtime\nfunctions, grant JavaScript `[[Construct]]`, turn a generator into an\nordinary returning function, or add a source feature a frontend refuses.\nConstructors and asynchronous operations keep their declared source\nsemantics; ordinary callability does not imply either capability.\n\n#### 8.10.2 Callable representation and identity\n\nKeep the callable's existing identity and source-specific data. Add the\ncommon entry beside its private code and metadata:\n\n```clojure\n;; Illustrative contents of one task-owned Python function cell.\n;; `entry` and `body-code` are live Yin closures, not literal AST maps.\n{:yang.call/entry entry\n :py/type :function\n :spec parameter-spec\n :defaults defaults\n :code body-code}\n```\n\nThe existing `:code` field is not the shared entry: its signature differs\nbetween preludes. It may remain private. Cross-language callers must not\ninspect it or extract it to bypass the entry.\n\nA cell-backed callable stores the entry in its cell contents. An\nimmutable callable descriptor, such as a bound method, may carry it\ndirectly in its map. The common prelude projects the entry structurally:\nread an existing sealed cell reference through `cell/get`, or inspect\nthe immutable descriptor, then obtain `:yang.call/entry`. It must not\ndispatch on `:py/type`, `:js/type`, `:php/type`, language names, or a\nregistry of languages.\n\nAn admitted callable is a runtime cell/descriptor constructed or exposed\nby the callable constructors or import/export projections of a pinned,\nconforming profile. The entry slot is a runtime descriptor field, not a\nsource property that promotes arbitrary data to a function. A Python\ndictionary, JavaScript object, or PHP array containing a source key\nspelled `:yang.call/entry` remains ordinary source data unless an explicit\nprofile-defined projection makes it a callable descriptor. Source\nproperty access must not overwrite or masquerade as this runtime slot.\nThis is an obligation of construction and source resolution, not a new\nVM type, descriptor seal, or runtime provenance/language registry. Once\nthe resolved descriptor is admitted, the shared projection is structural;\nUAST deliberately constructing a conforming descriptor opts into the\nconvention rather than changing a source language's data-map semantics.\n\nMissing entry means not callable. Constructors must install a genuine\nunary Yin closure, and supported source mutations must preserve that\ninvariant. Unary arity is a constructor/profile conformance obligation,\nnot a signature introspection operation: Yin closures are opaque and the\nVM's existing argument binding does not enforce this convention's arity.\nA key in a map grants no VM privilege; application, ownership, and\neffect checks still apply. A non-applicable entry remains an operational\nVM application defect, not a source exception caught by the shared helper.\n\nFor callable kinds whose eligibility can change, the same cell or\ndescriptor may also contain `:yang.call/eligible?`, a unary Yin predicate\non the original callable. Without it, an entry is eligible by default.\nWith it, the common callable test uses its boolean result. The predicate\nreads explicit runtime metadata/heap only; it must not mutate state,\nevaluate arguments, execute the target body, or invoke getters/user hooks.\nIt has the same constructor/arity obligations as the entry. For example,\nan instance can keep one dispatch entry while eligibility follows whether\nits class currently supplies a supported call method; changing the class\ndoes not require rewriting every instance.\n\nCall eligibility is tested at the callability-check point required by\nthe caller's source, not universally before argument evaluation. The\nentry resolves/rechecks a dynamic target at its source-required dispatch\npoint so argument side effects that change eligibility remain visible.\nStatic callable kinds need no predicate.\n\nSource callable designators, such as PHP function-name strings and\ncallable arrays where supported, are resolved under their source's rules\nbefore common invocation. They do not gain entry slots merely by being\nstrings or arrays. Exporting a designator as a first-class callable needs\nan explicit frontend projection to an admitted descriptor, retaining any\nsource-required late lookup and receiver semantics. Passing the raw\nstring or array as data leaves it unchanged; a foreign caller must not\nguess its language or search an ambient namespace to invoke it. This is\nsource resolution/projection, not a language-pair wrapper around an\nalready admitted function.\n\nCross-language passage must not allocate a replacement function cell.\nReturned functions retain their original identity, captures, defaults,\nbound receiver, properties, and static state. A receiving frontend's\ncallable test follows this common eligibility rule rather than rejecting\nforeign native tags. Foreign attribute access and type reflection remain\nprofile-owned; callability grants no general right to interpret another\nruntime's cell layout.\n\nCompiler-internal lambdas and host functions do not acquire this\nconvention merely by being applicable in Yin. A source import exposing\none must emit an entry from its declared signature and effect profile.\nIt must not guess an opaque closure's signature or bypass host-effect\nand custody rules. Internal helper calls need not construct records.\n\n#### 8.10.3 Invocation record\n#### 8.10.9 Publication, visibility, and reproducibility\n\nShared callability creates no common global scope. An import or\ncomposition explicitly binds exports in the receiving source namespace\nunder its normal name/module rules. Missing names keep their source\nerrors. No fallback searches other frontends, the filesystem, a host\npackage registry, or ambient globals.\n\nLinked modules publish code and immutable specifications. Their bodies\ninstantiate function objects and common entries in the importing task,\nas section 8.5.6 requires. Install children must not export live function\ncells. A higher-order result is an ordinary runtime value, not a new\nlinker publication on each call.\n\nLowering/runtime profiles pin the implementation and binding/value\nextensions. Existing dependency/effect/custody checks remain. Type facts\nstay beside code under `yin.vm.typecheck`, not in lambda language tags.\nDo not duplicate existing lambda parameters in another persisted\nauthority over the private body signature.\n\nBefore admitting a compiled composition, its profile/dependency\ndeclarations must establish one compatible convention revision for the\nentries it exposes. An incompatible revision needs an explicitly pinned\nprojection or is refused before execution. Neither a common slot name nor\nan opaque runtime closure proves revision compatibility. No runtime\nlanguage registry or inspection of captured environments supplies it.\n\nChanged entry code changes code identities through the normal encoder.\nRetain source, lowered UAST, pinned profiles, and projections under\nexisting provenance/unitarity rules. A fast path may omit the record\nonly after proving equivalent evaluation, binding, foreign callability,\nexceptions, effects, suspension, and identity. Correctness must not\n(ns yang.php.antlr.e2e-test\n  \"End to end on the JVM: source -> CST packet -> lowering stage -> program\n   envelope -> the bundled program on each of the four VMs (the AST walker,\n   the semantic, stack and register VMs). Every fixture of\n   `yang.php.antlr.programs` prints the same text on all four.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as cst]\n    [yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness :as h]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\n    [yang.php.antlr.packets :as packets]\n    [yang.php.antlr.packets-p3b :as packets-p3b]\n    [yang.php.antlr.permutations :as perms]\n    [yang.php.antlr.phpt :as phpt]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs :as programs]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p3b :as p3b]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.e2e-test :as ts]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(def ^:private vms [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\n\n\n(defn- rendered\n  \"The text `fixture` prints: `:out`, then the fatal line of an `:uncaught`.\"\n  [{:keys [out uncaught]}]\n  (str out\n       (when uncaught\n         (str \"PHP Fatal error:  Uncaught \" (:class uncaught) \": \" (:message uncaught)))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow fixtures-on-every-vm-test\n  (doseq [{:keys [id source] :as fixture} programs/fixtures\n          :let [out (rendered fixture)]]\n    (testing (name id)\n      (let [results (h/run-php source)]\n        (is (not (contains? results :diagnostics)) (pr-str results))\n        (doseq [k vms]\n          (is (= out (get results k)) (str (name id) \" on \" k)))))))\n\n\n(deftest fixtures-on-the-walker-test\n  (doseq [{:keys [id source out diag uncaught oracle]} programs/fixtures\n          :let [r (h/run-raw source)]]\n    (is (not= :pending oracle) (name id))\n    (is (= out (h/latin1->text (:php/out r))) (name id))\n    (is (= (vec diag) (mapv (juxt :errno :message) (:php/diag r))) (name id))\n    (is (= uncaught (some-> (:php/uncaught r) (select-keys [:class :message])))\n        (name id))))\n\n\n(defn- app?\n  [node op]\n  (and (map? node)\n       (= :application (:type node))\n       (= {:type :variable, :name op} (:operator node))))\n\n\n(defn- lowered-ts\n  [source]\n  (let [{:keys [program diagnostics]} (ts/lower-source source :bundled)]\n    (assert (nil? diagnostics) (pr-str diagnostics))\n    (let [{:yin/keys [batch root]} program]\n      (nth batch root))))\n\n\n(defn- export-projection\n  \"The donor program followed by its explicitly named global export read.\"\n  [donor export-name]\n  (u/then donor (u/sexp->uast (list 'js/global-get {:js/str export-name}))))\n\n\n(defn- install-php-function-export\n  \"Project `%foreign` into PHP's function namespace before the source body.\n   The lowered PHP call and its resolve/call nodes remain untouched.\"\n  [ast export-name]\n  (let [projection (u/sexp->uast\n                     (list 'cell/set! 'php.rt/functions\n                           (list 'assoc\n                                 '(cell/get php.rt/functions)\n                                 export-name\n                                 '%foreign)))\n        seen (volatile! false)\n        result (walk/postwalk\n                 (fn [node]\n                   (if (app? node 'php/run-main)\n                     (let [body (first (:operands node))]\n                       (assert (= :lambda (:type body)) \"php/run-main body is not a lambda\")\n                       (vreset! seen true)\n                       (assoc node :operands [(update body :body #(u/then projection %))]))\n                     node))\n                 ast)]\n    (assert @seen \"PHP program has no php/run-main application\")\n    result))\n\n\n(defn- run-with-ts-export\n  [donor-source export-name php-source]\n  (let [donor (lowered-ts donor-source)\n        {:keys [ast diagnostics]} (h/lower-program php-source)\n        _ (assert (nil? diagnostics) (pr-str diagnostics))\n        php-ast (install-php-function-export ast export-name)\n        composition {:type :application,\n                     :operator {:type :lambda,\n                                :params ['%foreign],\n                                :body php-ast},\n                     :operands [(export-projection donor export-name)]}\n        result (vm/value (vm/eval (tu/create-vm {:modules (php-h/host-registry)})\n                                  composition))]\n    (h/render result)))\n\n\n(deftest real-lowered-ts-export-called-from-php-test\n  (testing \"unmodified PHP source calls a published TS global export through yang.call\"\n    (is (= \"4\"\n           (run-with-ts-export\n             \"globalThis.donor = (x, y) => x + y;\"\n             \"donor\"\n             \"<?php echo donor(1.5, 2.5);\")))))\n\n\n(deftest real-lowered-php-callback-round-trip-test\n  (testing \"TS stores and calls the received PHP closure, then returns the same cell\"\n    (is (= \"calledsame\"\n           (run-with-ts-export\n             (str \"globalThis.accept = (f) => {\"\n                  \" globalThis.stored = f;\"\n                  \" globalThis.stored(7);\"\n                  \" return globalThis.stored;\"\n                  \"};\")\n             \"accept\"\n             (str \"<?php $cb = function($x) {\"\n                  \" echo 'called'; return $x + 1;\"\n                  \"};\"\n                  \"$returned = accept($cb);\"\n                  \"echo ($returned === $cb ? 'same' : 'different');\"))))))\n\n\n(deftest packets-match-source-test\n  (doseq [[id form] packets/forms\n          :let [{:keys [source]} (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) programs/fixtures))]]\n    (is (= form (h/packet->form (cst/parse-source source))) (name id))))\n\n\n(defn- matrix-rows\n  [out]\n  (let [[eq sp] (str/split-lines out)\n        w (count programs/matrix-values)]\n    {:eq (mapv #(apply str %) (partition w eq)),\n     :sp (mapv #(apply str (map {\\0 \"<\", \\1 \"=\", \\2 \">\"} %)) (partition w sp))}))\n\n\n(deftest scalar-comparison-matrix-test\n  (let [{:keys [eq sp]} (matrix-rows (h/run-walker programs/matrix-source))]\n    (is (= programs/equal-matrix eq))\n    (is (= programs/spaceship-matrix sp))\n    (testing \"cells reasoned from the manual, independent of the golden\"\n      (let [idx (zipmap programs/matrix-values (range))]\n        (doseq [[a b eq? cmp] programs/known-cells\n                :let [i (idx a), j (idx b)]]\n          (is (= (if eq? \\1 \\0) (get-in eq [i j])) (str a \" == \" b))\n          (is (= (get {-1 \\<, 0 \\=, 1 \\>} cmp) (get-in sp [i j])) (str a \" <=> \" b)))))))\n\n\n(deftest float-text-test\n  (let [src (str \"<?php\\n\"\n                 (apply str (for [[lit] programs/float-cases]\n                              (str \"echo \" lit \", \\\"|\\\"; var_dump(\" lit \");\\n\"))))\n        expected (str (apply str (for [[_ echo dump] programs/float-cases]\n                                   (str echo \"|float(\" dump \")\\n\"))))]\n    (is (= expected (h/run-walker src)))))\n\n\n(deftest refusals-are-named-test\n  (doseq [[source construct]\n          [[\"<?php $a = &f();\" :reference-source]\n           [\"<?php $$a[0] = 1;\" :assignment-target]\n           [\"<?php function f(int ...$a) {}\" :typed-variadic]\n           [\"<?php function f(&...$a) {}\" :variadic-reference]\n           [\"<?php $a = &new B;\" :reference]\n           [\"<?php static $a = 1;\" :static]\n           [\"<?php echo FOO;\" :constant]\n           [\"<?php echo \\\"a$b[0]\\\";\" :interpolation]\n           [\"<?php echo \\\"a$b->c\\\";\" :interpolation]\n           [\"<?php echo (array)1;\" :cast/array]\n           [\"<?php $o = new class { public $x = 1; };\" :anonymous-class]]\n          :when construct]\n    (let [{:keys [diagnostics]} (h/run-php source)\n          d (first diagnostics)]\n      (is (= :yang.php/unsupported (:yang.php/diagnostic d)) source)\n      (is (= construct (:construct d)) source))))\n\n\n(deftest leading-numeric-string-warns-test\n  (let [r (h/run-raw \"<?php echo \\\"5 apples\\\" + 1;\")]\n    (is (= \"6\" (:php/out r)))\n    (is (= [{:php.diag/warning true,\n             :errno 2,\n             :message \"A non-numeric value encountered\"}]\n           (:php/diag r)))\n    (is (nil? (:php/uncaught r))))\n  (testing \"a well formed numeric string does not warn\"\n    (is (= [] (:php/diag (h/run-raw \"<?php echo \\\" 5 \\\" + 1;\"))))))\n\n\n(deftest pow-fractional-refusal-test\n  (testing \"G-pow-frac: a fractional exponent refuses at run time, with the ledger id\"\n    (let [r (h/run-raw \"<?php echo 2 ** 0.5;\")]\n      (is (= \"Error\" (-> r :php/uncaught :class)))\n      (is (= \"** with a fractional exponent is not supported yet (yang.php known gap G-pow-frac)\"\n             (-> r :php/uncaught :message))))))\n\n\n(deftest compile-errors-are-named-test\n  (doseq [[source fragment]\n          [[\"<?php break;\" \"'break' not in the 'loop' or 'switch' context\"]\n           [\"<?php function f() { while (1) { } break; }\"\n            \"'break' not in the 'loop' or 'switch' context\"]\n           [\"<?php while (1) { break 0; }\" \"'break' operator accepts only positive integers\"]\n           [\"<?php while (1) { continue 0; }\" \"'continue' operator accepts only positive integers\"]\n           [\"<?php while (1) { break 2; }\" \"Cannot 'break' 2 levels\"]\n           [\"<?php while (1) { while (1) { continue 3; } }\" \"Cannot 'continue' 3 levels\"]\n           [\"<?php while (1) { break; } while (1) { break 2; }\" \"Cannot 'break' 2 levels\"]\n           [\"<?php $n = 1; while (1) { break $n; }\" \"non-integer operand\"]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:15:     `break`/`continue` are `php/call-ec` escapes bound to `%brk<id>` and\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:21:     are hoisted. `return` is an escape from `php/call-ec`, bound only when\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:32:     `(let [%f (php/resolve-fn \\\"f\\\" \\\"F\\\")] (php/call %f [a b]))`.\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:1601:                 (app* 'php/call-with-binding-profile\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:1605:                   (app* 'php/call-named f pos named)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:1606:                   (app* 'php/call f pos))))))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:1717:                          (core/site :call (app* 'php/call (u/v f) (args-vector nodes)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:1778:                                            (app* 'php/callable-in acc (cc-node ctx))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:1787:                  (app* 'php/callable-in (callee-value ctx n fname) (cc-node ctx))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:1803:                      (app* 'php/resolve-fn2 (u/lit primary-lc) (u/lit fallback-lc) (u/lit written))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:1804:                      (app* 'php/resolve-fn (u/lit lc) (u/lit written)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:2011:                      (app* 'php/callable-in acc (cc-node ctx))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:2255:  \"`node` under a `php/call-ec` that binds the frame's `kind` escape, when the\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:2259:    (app* 'php/call-ec (u/lam [(get frame kind)] node))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3092:        body (if has-return? (app* 'php/call-ec (u/lam ['%ret] body)) body)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3667:     (app* 'php/call-ec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:29:     function        a cell {:php/type :function :name s :code (fn [args])\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:30:                             :yang.call/entry (fn [invocation])}\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:231:    [php/call-ec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:291:               (php/call (php/callable-fn h)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2110:     ;; unary entry. `:yang.call/callee` supplies self, preserving cell identity.\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2112:       (let [f (cell/new (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :php/type :function) :name name)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2118:           (cell/set! f (assoc (cell/get f) :yang.call/entry\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2120:                                 (let [callee (get invocation :yang.call/callee)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2121:                                       positional (get invocation :yang.call/positional)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2122:                                       named (get invocation :yang.call/named)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2123:                                       binding-profile (get invocation :yang.call/binding-profile)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2135:                                     ((get invocation :yang.call/raise)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2136:                                      {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/unsupported-binding\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2137:                                       :yang.call/data\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2138:                                       {:yang.call/binding-profile binding-profile}}))))))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2225:    [php/resolve-fn\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2234:    [php/call\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2236:       ((get (cell/get f) :yang.call/entry)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2237:        (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/callee f)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2238:                             :yang.call/positional args)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2239:                      :yang.call/named [])\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2240:               :yang.call/raise (fn [condition] (php/raise condition)))))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2241:    [php/call-with-binding-profile\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2243:       ((get (cell/get f) :yang.call/entry)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2244:        (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/callee f)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2245:                                    :yang.call/positional args)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2246:                             :yang.call/named named)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2247:                      :yang.call/raise (fn [condition] (php/raise condition)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2248:               :yang.call/binding-profile binding-profile)))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2384:                   (if (php/callable? v) v :php/undef)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2390:    [php/callable?\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2498:                         (php/callable? v)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3266:           (php/call (php/bind-method m this static) args)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3267:           (php/call-named (php/bind-method m this static)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3524:    [php/call-obj-method\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3685:           (do (php/call-value (get (get fns i) 0) (get (get fns i) 1))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4001:         (php/call (get bound :php