{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_141","type":"agent_message","text":"Committed as `edc50134` — `fix(yang.php): admit foreign yang.call cells`. **Not pushed.**\n\nPHP now admits conforming foreign callable cells through the shared resolver and invocation path, and the linked PHP profile pins `yang.call`. The new PHP-source test stores a TS callback in an array, calls it, and verifies strict identity. Non-conforming function cells retain the undefined-function diagnostic.\n\nFocused callback, resolver, prelude, and direct-export tests passed; the linked-profile test passed on all three vector VMs. Class-model, objects, and generators passed (14 tests, 1,201 assertions). `cljstyle` and clj-kondo are clean.\n\nThe broad PHP e2e run still reports existing php-src selection mismatches and the `echo FOO` refusal expectation. The `gc_013` pin appears sound and the harness comparison matches its expected output; the likely mismatch is in the PHP GC engine. I could not verify against a PHP CLI oracle here, so the pin remains unchanged. Details are in the uncommitted [findings file](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4/collab/1793700000000-engineer-p4-foreign-admission.gpt-6-luna.findings.md)."}}
